# init.dolby_f5.rc - Fold5 DAP stack (in-tree).
# Mounts at post-fs-data, BEFORE the audio HAL starts, so no service restart
# is ever needed. Effect on/off stays with the stock QS tile
# (org.lineageos.dap), which toggles the DAP AudioEffect live, like stock.
# Opt out: touch /data/dolby_f5/disabled + reboot (stock stack stays).
#
# NOTE: uses exec (init's own context), NOT a service block: services need a
# seclabel-defined domain transition and init rejects shell_exec without one
# ("has incorrect label or no domain transition" - proven on 2026-09-15 boot).
# exec runs as init (u:r:init:s0, root) which can mount/chcon freely.

on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/dolby_f5 0755 root root
    exec - root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/bin/dolby_f5.sh mount

# boot_completed backstop: system rc triggers may register after early-boot
# triggers already fired (proven: post-fs-data block never ran on 0915
# release). Property triggers from /system/etc/init DO fire (audioserver.rc
# proves it). Script is idempotent: second run is a no-op.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    exec - root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/bin/dolby_f5.sh mount
